{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And I seized the two tablets\"</b> — this too is among the rebukes. He says: your sin was too great to bear, for when I saw you playing before the calf I could not restrain myself and I broke the tablets. And it was necessary to mention this in order that he may inform them of the matter of the second tablets, as he will explain. And it is possible that he further hints at the good that he did with them, for he endangered himself to break the tablets of Elohim for their benefit, as our Rabbis said (Shemot Rabbah 43:1): better that she be judged as an un betrothed woman and not as a married woman."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:00.159108446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}